      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, which is typically given as 850 mg three times daily. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum. 1700 may have been a typo for 850.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily**, or another dose below the maximum.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
